From 05e04c066a5350f85282e509e0ccc7c58b00eb8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:08:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): move-to-project shows the row in its new
 project at once [daveey]

Problem: moving a session into another project (row menu, drag, Cmd-Shift-P)
took several seconds to show the row in the destination.

Why 1: the sidebar files a row by $projectOwnerBySessionId, derived from the
  cached $projectTree, and the backend owner wins over the row's cwd
  (workspace-groups.ts liveSessionProjectId / overlayLiveLanes).
Why 2: moveSessionToProject changed that tree only via refreshProjectTree(),
  run AFTER the session.workspace.move RPC returned (plus projects.list /
  mkdir / projects.create round trips for a cross-gateway move).
Why 3: that refetch is GET /api/profiles/projects/tree, which takes 2-5 s on
  the hub (loop-watch: "slow request GET /api/profiles/projects/tree
  ?preview_limit=2000 2.1-5.0s", _read_serial_profile_db).
Root (happened): the move had no optimistic layer for ownership; only $sessions
  cwd was patched, and the authoritative-owner rule ignores cwd.
Root (not caught): move tests asserted the RPC sequence and scope, never what
  the sidebar shows while the RPC is pending.

Fix: store/projects-move-optimistic.ts reassigns the row in $projectTree (ids,
previews, lanes, counts) and patches its cwd before any RPC. Each tree payload
re-applies a pending move until the backend agrees (or 30 s), so a refresh
that read the backend before the move landed can't snap it back. A failed move
undoes both and refetches. The follow-suppression helpers moved there too to
keep projects.ts under its line ratchet.

Tests: projects-move-optimistic.test.ts (row in destination while the RPC is
pending, survives a stale refresh, rollback on failure, pure reassignment);
fails with the optimistic call removed. Cross-gateway sequence asserts now
ignore the rollback's projects.tree read.
